---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy · Mohakash"
  description="What Mohakash stores on your device, what it sends over the network, and what it never collects."
>
  <div class="page page--tight">
    <div class="stack-sm" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        Mohakash is a free, open-source astronomy reader and Android live wallpaper. It has no
        account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking.
      </p>
      <p class="muted-block">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="collect" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="collect">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 15px;">
        Nothing. We do not operate a user database, we do not ask for an email address, and we do
        not use analytics, crash-reporting or advertising SDKs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="device" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="device">What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-body); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
        <li>Your settings, such as Wi-Fi-only downloads, image scaling and the daily-update switch.</li>
        <li>Pictures and entry metadata that you save with the heart button.</li>
        <li>Cached API responses and downloaded images, so the app can work offline.</li>
        <li>The current wallpaper picture, stored in the app's private storage.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted-block">
        This information stays in the app's private storage. If Android backup is enabled on your
        device, Android may include app data in your own Google backup. That backup is controlled
        by your device settings, not by this project.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="network" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="network">Network requests</h2>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 15px;">
        The app and website fetch the public APOD JSON and the pictures from the original sources.
        Like any HTTP request, these requests include your IP address, user agent and the requested
        URL. They go to:
      </p>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-body); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
        <li><a href={SITE.publicApiBase}>GitHub Pages</a>, which serves this project's public API.</li>
        <li><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/">NASA Science</a>, which serves APOD metadata and images.</li>
        <li><a href={SITE.githubRepo}>GitHub</a>, when you open the source, issue tracker or a release link.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted-block">
        Those providers process requests under their own privacy policies. Mohakash does not add
        identifiers to the requests and does not send your saved pictures or settings anywhere.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="permissions" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="permissions">Android permissions</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-body); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
        <li><strong>Internet</strong> and <strong>network state</strong> — fetch the picture and API data, and respect Wi-Fi-only mode.</li>
        <li><strong>Notifications</strong> (optional) — tell you when the live wallpaper picture changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Storage</strong> (Android 7–9 only) — save a picture to your gallery. Android 10 and later use the system photo picker and need no storage permission.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="donate" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="donate">Donations</h2>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 15px;">
        The optional Donate link opens an external page and adds only a <code>source=Mohakash</code>
        query parameter so the project can see where a visit came from. No personal information is
        sent by Mohakash.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="children" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="children">Children</h2>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 15px;">
        Mohakash is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do
        not knowingly collect personal information from anyone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="changes" style="max-width: 68ch;">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="page-lead" style="font-size: 15px;">
        If this policy changes, the new version will be published at this address with a new date.
        Questions or corrections are welcome in the <a href={SITE.issuesUrl}>issue tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
